      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name} - The way that I expected the node to function would be: \n\nThe given audio is scaled in speed to the animation being played. If the animation is 2x the speed, it would be expected to be played at a similar rate\n\nThe given offset for enter-delay in seconds would be expected to be scaled by the nodes speed\n\nIt can be argued that this is a feature request, but I find it somewhat confusing that something on an animation node would not adhere to the \"general rules\" of that node (ie. scaling)",
